{
  "note": "📚️ The ONE boot-example rule both shells answer. React: `🐚️Shell/🟦️.tsx` `resolveBootExampleId`. wgpu: `🐚️Shell/🎯️targets/🧊️wgpu/🦀️.rs` `resolve_boot_example_id`, driven from `sync_session_chrome`. `defaultExampleId` is the per-server seed (`VITE_SEMIO_DEFAULT_EXAMPLE`) OR the per-navigation `?example=` query, which is why an id no option carries must fall back rather than fault: a url is not a place to hard-fail a shell.",
  "bootQueryParam": "example",
  "rows": [
